WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.080
- I want to be completely honest with you.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.000
If you plan to stay in
consulting for the long-term,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.590
you will be not set up well
for a general management career.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.320
You will lack crucial
skills that are required

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.880
to run large organizations

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.220
that you will not build in consulting,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.940
even if you work for a
leading strategy consulting firm

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.040
such as McKinsey, BCG, or Bain.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.590
Hi guys, my name is Heinrich

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.620
and welcome to another
coffee break with me

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.500
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.130
On this channel I want to
help you to become successful

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.150
in the first years of your career.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.970
I do that by drawing from my experience,

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.780
having worked at McKinsey as
consultant for several years

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.370
and now in a C-level position
at a German retailer.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.100
Today I'm talking about the downsides

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.240
of working in consulting,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.210
and here I'm not
referring to the lifestyle

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.290
or to the work-life balance
or anything like that.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.140
But I'm talking about the
things that you do not learn

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.160
if you work in a consulting firm.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.390
You know that I'm quite
positive about my time

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.680
in consulting at McKinsey,

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.580
and I even made a whole video about

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.070
why I believe that consulting
is the right first career step

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.730
for most business graduates
fresh out of university.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.120
If you have not seen that yet,

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.130
I will insert a link to that
video somewhere above here.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.430
Check it out because I really
believe that consulting

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.950
is a great opportunity
for most of you out there.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.160
After I made this first
video about consulting,

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.020
you reached out to me and you asked me

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.510
to do this other video as well.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.370
To also talk about the downsides,

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.330
and you know that if you ask
me I will deliver for you.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.960
So before I tell you the three things

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.400
that I believe you will
not learn in consulting,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.790
please like the video
for the YouTube algorithm

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.850
if you're getting any
value out of it at all.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.730
And please also subscribe to my channel

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.980
to stay up to date with
all my video updates.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.420
I will release at least
one video every week

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.240
and if you wanna get even
more content from me,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.800
follow me on my Instagram.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.530
The handle is @firmlearning

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.460
on my Instagram I'm posting
new content for your daily

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.540
to help you to become

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.210
successful in the first
years of your career.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.210
But this does not mean
that working in consulting

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.070
is like a fairy tale and
you will learn everything

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.490
you need for your future.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.870
And specifically I believe
there are three things,

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.460
three very important
skills and capabilities

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.940
that you will not build

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.250
if you stay in consulting
for the longterm.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.760
My career recommendation
therefore is that yes,

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.130
a few years in consulting

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.270
will make a lot of sense for most people,

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.780
but after a couple of years in consulting.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.010
It is probably not a bad idea

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.250
to look for a more operational role

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.910
to build your full skill set.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.240
But let's now dive into it.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.820
Let's talk about the top three things

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.820
that you do not learn in consulting

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.260
and these are not some minor things,

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.880
but these are things that I
believe are really crucial

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.090
and are really important for you

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.530
to become a well rounded general manager.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.540
The first aspect is team leadership,

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.420
and here I wanna mention that
there are two facets of that.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.236
So the one facet is the positive facet

00:02:35.236 --> 00:02:38.350
because the positive side of
working in consulting is that

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.910
pretty quickly after
only a couple of years

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.640
of being a regular consultant,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.070
you will usually advance into
the rank of a project lead.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.200
And this will mean that
you will be responsible

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.430
of a team of usually two
to four other consultants

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.760
working on the ground at the
client site on your project.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.420
And this is an opportunity
for team leadership experience

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.840
that you will get much quicker,

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.460
than compared to most
other industry roles

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.160
where usually it takes much
longer until you really get

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.760
team leadership responsibility
for a team of people

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:07.610
in your company.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.260
So why this is the positive
side of team leadership

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.440
when you work in consulting.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.450
The other facet is

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.830
what type of team leadership
experience you get.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.680
So here you need to think
about what types of people,

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.580
what types of colleagues you will lead,

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.070
especially if you work for one of the

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:23.890
leading consulting firms
such as McKinsey, BCG or Bain

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.590
or MBB as they're also often referred to.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.830
Pretty much all of the people
that you are working with

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.010
in these firms are so
called high potentials.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.460
This means that they are graduates

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.840
from leading universities
around the world.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.090
Most of them ranked in the top
10% of their university class.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.750
Many of them had highly
competitive scholarships,

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.420
they have already
collected work experience

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.900
in high profile internships.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.690
And most of them have quite impressive

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.150
extracurriculars as well.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.330
These are the people
that may be your team,

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.930
and this means that your team
will be just highly motivated

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.370
whenever you just tip them

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.920
in one direction as a project lead,

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.030
they will run,

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.200
they will work day and night for you.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.650
They will do whatever they can

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.420
to get a good result for
the client and for the team.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.980
While I do not want to say
that being a project lead

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.870
at an MBB consulting
firm is an easy endeavor,

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.080
leading and motivating
your consulting colleagues

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.260
is probably not one of
the most challenging

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.700
leadership activities out there.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.890
If you then later want to
transition into industry

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.970
or startup into a more
general manager type of role,

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.770
the situation that you
will find yourself in

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.390
will be significantly different.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.710
And while of course in industry

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.530
you can find some highly capable,

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.690
motivated and professional
colleagues as well,

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.250
it is fair to say that you will
meet and you will work with

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.570
many people who are
significantly less motivated,

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.470
significantly less driven
than your average colleague

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.947
at an MBB consulting firm.

00:04:38.947 --> 00:04:40.200
And this is now where

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.360
your real leadership
abilities need to shine.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.390
This is really a challenge

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.890
and this is what you need to learn

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.220
to succeed in such a role.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.850
For most of your consulting colleagues

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.020
while you're in consulting,

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.800
the work, at least within the workweek

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.470
is the priority number one.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.860
But the average person in
industry maybe has a family,

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.720
maybe has other life priorities as well,

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.350
and this is completely fine
and completely understandable.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:00.640
But you just need to recognize

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.390
as a leader that the mindset of the people

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.400
that you work with will
just be a different one,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.450
and you need to adapt to that

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.420
and to change your
leadership style accordingly.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.360
And for these reasons,

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.420
I believe that the team
leadership experience

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.200
that you get when working in consulting

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.480
it's not worthless,

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.310
but it's not directly applicable

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:17.800
to a regular industry or startup context.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.274
Leading MBB consulting
teams is really not the same

00:05:20.274 --> 00:05:23.760
as working with a large
organization of 20, 30, 40 people,

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.870
with a big variety of
educational backgrounds

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:26.859
and skill sets.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.210
You really need to get this
broader leadership experience

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.870
firsthand to become a well
rounded business professional.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.620
The second thing that you're
not learning in consulting

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:35.560
is Operations.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.160
In your daily work as a consultant

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.240
there's a clear lack of focus
on operational activities.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.600
What do I mean by that?

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.517
If you work in consulting,

00:05:43.517 --> 00:05:46.790
and this is especially true
for MBB strategy consulting,

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:49.800
but also for most other types
of consulting engagements,

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.390
what you deliver in the end?

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:54.840
Our concepts, our strategies
in the end of course

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.050
you also wanna help your client

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.600
implement the things that you recommend,

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.630
but the deliverables that you leave

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.480
will usually be pieces of
papers, they're concepts.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.580
As a consultant you usually walk around

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.490
with the mindset that the difficult

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:09.380
the challenging part is to
come up with these concepts

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.230
that you develop.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.610
And then the execution,

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.120
well that's for the other people to do

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.150
this is just about implementing
what you told them to do.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.740
It's not especially difficult
or challenging, right?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.870
Though the truth is that as a consultant

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:24.180
you are often significantly
underestimating

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.180
how difficult it is to really execute.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.330
To really implement these ideas

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.760
and I want to illustrate
that with a little example

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.340
that I experienced myself

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.020
when then later I transitioned
from the consulting role

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.920
into an operational role in industry.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:40.300
I was responsible for
an eCommerce operation

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.720
and we wanted to introduce
PayPal as a way of payment

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:44.960
in the online store.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.920
How would you do that as a consultant?

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.420
Probably you would write a report

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.060
in which you recommend a couple of things

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:51.140
that the client should do.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:52.940
And then one of the things
you could improve on

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.970
would be to offer a larger
variety of payment options

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:56.940
for your clients.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.750
And then probably in one bullet point,

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.320
you would write that
PayPal should be introduced

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.550
as a payment option.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:03.770
And when I was a consultant,

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.460
I probably would have thought
that implementing PayPal

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.930
would take you one or two weeks,

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:08.930
maybe three weeks

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.430
if there were some big
unexpected problems coming up.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.450
But implementing PayPal
as a payment option

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.750
should be rather easy.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.500
So this was the mindset that I
had when I worked in industry

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.410
and I wanted now to implement PayPal

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.500
as new payment option
for our online store.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.600
And then I learned what
all of this really meant.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.010
This meant that we needed
to implement new interfaces

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.950
between our online eCommerce solution

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.940
and the accounting system
that we were using.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.730
We needed to work together
with external service providers

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:35.990
to make sure that this
interface was running smoothly.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.590
Then we found out that the
legacy accounting system

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.900
that we were using was not able to support

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.890
an additional way of payment.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:45.740
It had a fixed number of
slots for payment options

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.400
that you could use and implement,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.950
but these were already taken

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.430
so you couldn't just set
up a new way of payment.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:53.170
So now we needed to find a workaround

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:55.020
in the accounting system in order for us

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:57.440
to now implement payment
as a new payment option.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.920
Then there were also some
struggles with PayPal itself

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:00.910
because we needed to include

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.830
different types of bank accounts.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.010
And we found out that the person

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:06.420
who initially set up the
PayPal account needed to be

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.410
the exact person on which the bank account

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.440
then was set as well.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.080
And this alone took us weeks

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.340
until we figured it out
with the PayPal support

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:15.870
that all the accounts were
registered with the right names

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:16.900
and everything was running

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.440
on the PayPal end the way it should.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.130
So instead of only one or two weeks

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.750
before we could offer
PayPal to our customers,

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.360
it took us more than three months

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.470
before we really were able to offer PayPal

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.120
as a payment option to our customers.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.510
As a consultant, you do
not see these things.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.180
You regularly significantly underestimate

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:35.930
the pain and the
difficulties of implementing

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.180
the suggestions that you make,

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.850
and when you then later
transition into an industry role,

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.850
this will fall on your feet badly.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.350
You're just not used
to implement your ideas

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:47.030
to execute your ideas
and this is a problem.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.390
This is the type of experience

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:50.590
that you only get in an operational role

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.610
and you don't get this
exposure working in consulting.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.390
The third thing that in my opinion,

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.600
you do not learn properly
from working in consulting,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.780
is the value of agility and speed.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.990
Usually especially if you work at MBB,

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:04.570
but also other consulting firms,

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.850
you work for rather large corporations.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.570
You learn how to align things

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.570
with lots of different stakeholders.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.030
You learn how the
decision making processes

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.920
in these kinds of companies work,

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.600
and of course this is a
valuable skill in itself

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:19.870
But especially if you later
want to work in a startup

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.510
or in a smaller company
in these companies,

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:23.880
other things are important.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.030
These companies often
put a lot of emphasis

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.900
on the Silicon Valley value of moving fast

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.120
and breaking things.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.400
And it's often better to
just getting things done

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.860
than getting them right perfectly.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.740
And this of course is not the mindset

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.460
that large corporations have.

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:40.500
Also because of their size and
because of other implications

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.630
if things go wrong and the
rigor of internal alignment

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.440
and quality assurance processes.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.670
These companies often
teach you to be cautious,

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.280
to be sure that your cover your back,

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:52.370
that you made sure that you
checked all the possible things

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.350
that could go wrong before you
come up with a new concept,

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:57.350
and then propose it to
the senior management.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.640
In the smaller companies,

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.810
being thorough and being diligent

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.140
in this way is often not that important.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.050
You need to be fast,

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:04.883
you need to be quick,

00:10:04.883 --> 00:10:06.050
you need to be agile,

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:07.430
you need to do five things

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.510
and then be okay if two things don't work,

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:10.900
but the other three things do.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:11.740
And this is a skill

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.960
that requires a certain street smartness,

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.450
a certain way of doing things,

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:18.370
which doesn't put focus
so much on being polished,

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:19.560
on being corporate,

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.890
but just getting things done.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.070
And this is the agile startup mentality

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:23.903
that you will lack

00:10:23.903 --> 00:10:26.250
from working in most
consultancies out there.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.080
But that is so valuable for
many many roles out there.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.870
Many companies, especially if
you wanna work for a startup

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.780
or smaller company and not for
a big corporate in the end.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.220
So these were the three things

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.060
that you do not learn in consulting,

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:39.750
first team leadership,

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.350
second focus on operation and third,

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.120
the agility and the startup mindset

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.700
that you will just not have in the way

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.340
that you will have it in other companies.

